    {
      "id": "note-overview",
      "type": "note",
      "position": {
        "x": -680,
        "y": -300
      },
      "data": {
        "noteKind": "text",
        "noteContent": "Glorot and Bengio, \"Understanding the difficulty of training deep feedforward neural networks\", AISTATS 2010. Claim: with the standard initialisation, a deep network of sigmoid units saturates and its gradients shrink, so training stalls on a plateau; ReLU units (Nair and Hinton, ICML 2010) keep the gradient flowing. Recipe: two MLPs with 4 hidden layers of 128 units, Sigmoid in one and ReLU in the other, on 5,000 MNIST images, SGD lr 0.05 with momentum 0.9 for 10 epochs, log_grad_norm on. Under seed 0 on a CPU the sigmoid net's loss only moves from 2.35 to 2.30 (test accuracy 0.11, the share of the most common digit) and its gradient norm averages 0.21 over the second half of training. The ReLU net's loss falls from 1.66 to 0.20 (test accuracy 0.91) with a gradient norm of 1.30.\n\nGlorot 與 Bengio，〈Understanding the difficulty of training deep feedforward neural networks〉，AISTATS 2010。論點：用標準初始化時，由 sigmoid 單元組成的深層網路會飽和、梯度變小，訓練卡在平台上；ReLU 單元（Nair 與 Hinton，ICML 2010）能讓梯度繼續流動。配方：兩個各有 4 個 128 單元隱藏層的 MLP，一個用 Sigmoid、一個用 ReLU，在 5,000 張 MNIST 影像上用 SGD（lr 0.05、momentum 0.9）訓練 10 個 epoch，並開啟 log_grad_norm。在 CPU 上以種子 0 執行，sigmoid 網路的損失只從 2.35 動到 2.30（測試準確率 0.11，就是最常見數字所占的比例），訓練後半段的梯度範數平均 0.21。ReLU 網路的損失從 1.66 降到 0.20（測試準確率 0.91），梯度範數為 1.30。",
        "noteColor": "#3d3d1a",
        "boundToNodeId": "start",
        "boundOffset": {
          "x": -420,
          "y": 0
        },
        "noteWidth": 360
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "note-data",
      "type": "note",
      "position": {
        "x": 1000,
        "y": -300
      },
      "data": {
        "noteKind": "text",
        "noteContent": "MNIST ships with the repository under backend/data, so the run reads it from disk. DatasetSplit keeps a fixed 5,000 of the 60,000 training images; its own seed (0) picks them, so every arm trains on the same images through the one DataLoader.\n\nMNIST 隨專案放在 backend/data 底下，執行時直接從磁碟讀取。DatasetSplit 從 60,000 張訓練影像中固定留下 5,000 張，挑哪幾張由它自己的種子（0）決定，所以每一組都透過同一個 DataLoader 在同一批影像上訓練。",
        "noteColor": "#3d3d1a",
        "boundToNodeId": "dl-train",
        "boundOffset": {
          "x": 320,
          "y": 0
        },
        "noteWidth": 300
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "note-arms",
      "type": "note",
      "position": {
        "x": -300,
        "y": 1400
      },
      "data": {
        "noteKind": "text",
        "noteContent": "Each arm has its own SequentialModel node. One model node wired into two TrainingLoops would hand every loop the same weights, and each loop would continue from what the previous one left. The run seed (0, stored in the file) fixes the shuffle order, any dropout masks and each model's initial weights. Every node is seeded from the run seed and its own id, so the arms start from different draws of the same initialisation. With Persist weights between runs on (Settings > Training Behavior), a second Run continues from the trained weights; turn it off to repeat these numbers.\n\n每一組都有自己的 SequentialModel 節點。如果一個模型節點同時接到兩個 TrainingLoop，每個迴圈拿到的是同一份權重，後跑的會接著前一個留下的結果繼續訓練。執行種子（0，存在檔案裡）固定了洗牌順序、dropout 遮罩和每個模型的初始權重。每個節點的種子由執行種子和節點自己的 id 推得，所以各組的初始權重是同一種初始化方式下的不同抽樣。在設定 > 訓練行為中開啟「在多次執行間保留權重」時，第二次執行會從訓練過的權重繼續；關閉它才能重現這些數字。",
        "noteColor": "#3d3d1a",
        "boundToNodeId": "model-relu",
        "boundOffset": {
          "x": -340,
          "y": 0
        },
        "noteWidth": 300
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "note-model",
      "type": "note",
      "position": {
        "x": -300,
        "y": 400
      },
      "data": {
        "noteKind": "text",
        "noteContent": "Open the layer editor: Flatten -> four blocks of Linear -> Sigmoid (128 units) -> Linear 128->10. The model below has ReLU in place of each Sigmoid. PyTorch initialises every Linear from U(-1/sqrt(n), 1/sqrt(n)), n being its input width, which is the standard initialisation the paper starts from. The paper's remedy, its normalised initialisation, has no switch on SequentialModel, so this graph shows the problem and the ReLU fix.\n\n打開圖層編輯器：Flatten -> 四個 Linear -> Sigmoid 區塊（128 個單元）-> Linear 128->10。下面那個模型把每個 Sigmoid 換成 ReLU。PyTorch 用 U(-1/sqrt(n), 1/sqrt(n)) 初始化每個 Linear，n 是輸入寬度，這正是論文出發點的標準初始化。論文提出的解法是正規化初始化，SequentialModel 沒有這個選項，所以這張圖呈現的是問題本身和 ReLU 這個解法。",
        "noteColor": "#3d3d1a",
        "boundToNodeId": "model-sigmoid",
        "boundOffset": {
          "x": -340,
          "y": 0
        },
        "noteWidth": 300
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "note-grad-norm",
      "type": "note",
      "position": {
        "x": 1960,
        "y": 400
      },
      "data": {
        "noteKind": "text",
        "noteContent": "Both TrainingLoops have log_grad_norm on: every 10th optimizer step (log_interval) they record the total gradient norm as the grad_norm series. Open the run in the Runs panel to chart it for each loop. The sigmoid net's norm stays small while its loss sits near 2.30, the loss of a uniform guess; the ReLU net's stays several times larger while its loss falls.\n\n兩個 TrainingLoop 都開啟了 log_grad_norm：每 10 個最佳化步驟（log_interval）把整體梯度範數記成 grad_norm 序列。在執行任務面板打開這次執行，就能看到每個迴圈的圖表。sigmoid 網路的範數一直很小，損失停在 2.30 附近，也就是平均亂猜的損失；ReLU 網路的範數大了好幾倍，損失持續下降。",
        "noteColor": "#3d3d1a",
        "boundToNodeId": "viz-sigmoid",
        "boundOffset": {
          "x": 320,
          "y": 0
        },
        "noteWidth": 300
      }
    }
  ],
